board type: Freeride-Powder
rider level: Advanced
flex: 8/10
shape: Tapered Directional (tail narrower than nose for enhanced control and stability in deeper snow)
camber type: Surfy CamRock (camber between feet with rocker in tip and slightly in tail, plenty of pop with catch-free turns)
width: Standard, Wide
mounting pattern: 2x4 Inserts
available lengths: 152cm, 158cm, 164cm Wide
flagship status: Considered Nidecker's flagship board
topsheet: Absorbnid Topsheet (innovative top layer designed to absorb unwanted vibrations)
laminate: N-Tech 2.0 Construction with Triax Plus Fiberglass (combines cap and sandwich construction; fiberglass woven at three directions at 45°; multiple densities above and below core)
core: Mega Core with Carbon Cell (blend of poplar and paulownia with extra layers of vertically orientated glass fiber)
carbon technology: Carbon Cell (extra strip of carbon between feet for extra response and lightweight stability)
base: N-12000 Graphite (fastest base in Nidecker line, high density sintered with added graphite)
nose technology: Zero-G Nose (wood completely removed from part of nose, replaced with forged carbon for ultra light nose and extra powder float)
underfoot cushioning: Orbital Cushioning (shock absorbing TPU material surrounding inserts for smoother ride and eliminating foot fatigue)
edge reinforcement: Titanium Boosters (titanium inlays along edge underfoot near inserts for extra response edge to edge)
tail technology: Pow Diffuser (3D channels in tail for improved glide in deep snow, acts like funnel to spray snow out)
core milling: 3DN Concept (3D milled core between inserts for more precise flex underfoot and extra control)
insert configuration: 6+1 Inserts (traditional 4x2 pattern plus extra set towards tail for further setback)
